<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong to build Indonesia flats.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong to build Indonesia flats.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ssangyong Engineering and Construction, an unlisted unit of South Korea's Ssangyong Group, has received an order worth $57 million to build a luxury condominium complex in Jakarta, the company said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>A Ssangyong statement said the company had received the order from City Developments Ltd Group, a unit of the Singapore-based Hong Leong Group.</p>
<p>Construction of the three building complex will begin in December and is expected to be completed in October 1998.</p>
<p>There will be a total of 398 flats in the complex.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
